{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-exo-15-1","title":"Exodus 15:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The song of Moses, Miriam, and Israel on their deliverance. 22 The people want water in the wilderness. 23 The waters at Marah are bitter, they murmur, Moses prays, and sweetens the waters by God's direction. 27 They encamp at Elim, where are twelve wells, and seventy palm trees.</p>\n<p>Then. Jud 5:1-31; 2Sa 22:1-51; Ps 106:12; 107:8,15,21,22; Isa 12:1-6 Isa 51:10,11; Re 15:3 for. 21; 14:17,18,27; 18:11; Col 2:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-2","title":"Exodus 15:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>strength. Ps 18:1,2; 27:1; 28:8; 59:17; 62:6,7; 118:14; Hab 3:17-19; Php 4:13 song. De 10:21; Ps 22:3; 109:1; 140:7; Re 15:3 my salvation. 14:13; 2Sa 22:51; Ps 68:20; Isa 12:2; 45:17; 49:6; Jer 3:23; Lu 1:77 Lu 2:30; Joh 4:22; Ac 4:12; Re 19:1 my God. 4:22; Ge 17:7; Ps 22:10; Jer 31:33; 32:38; Zec 13:9 an habitation. 40:34; Ge 28:21,22; 2Sa 7:5; 1Ki 8:13,27; Ps 132:5; Isa 66:1 2Co 5:19; Eph 2:22; Col 2:9 my father's God. 3:15,16 exalt him. 2Sa 22:47; Ps 18:46; 30:1; 34:3; 99:5,9; 118:28; 145:1; Isa 25:1 Joh 5:23; Php 2:11; Re 5:9-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-3","title":"Exodus 15:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>a man. Ps 24:8; 45:3; Re 19:11-21 name. 3:13,15; 6:3,6; Ps 83:18; Isa 42:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-4","title":"Exodus 15:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>14:13-28 chosen. 14:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-5","title":"Exodus 15:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>depths. 14:28; Eze 27:34; Jon 2:2; Mic 7:19; Mt 18:6 they. Ne 9:11; Jer 51:63,64; Re 18:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-6","title":"Exodus 15:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>right hand. 11; 1Ch 29:11,12; Ps 17:7; 44:3; 60:5; 74:11; 77:10; 89:8-13 Ps 98:1; 118:15,16; Isa 51:9; 52:10; Mt 6:13 dashed. Ps 2:9; Isa 30:14; Jer 13:14; Re 2:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-7","title":"Exodus 15:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>the greatness. 9:16; De 33:26; Ps 68:33; 148:13; Isa 5:16; Jer 10:6 them that. Isa 37:17,23,29,36,38; Mic 4:11; Na 1:9-12; Zec 2:8; 14:3,8 Ac 9:4 consumed. Ps 59:13; 83:13; Isa 5:24; 47:14; Na 1:10; Mal 4:1; Mt 3:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-8","title":"Exodus 15:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>blast. 14:21; 2Sa 22:16; Job 4:9; Isa 11:4; 37:7; 2Th 2:8 the floods. 14:22; Ps 78:13; Hab 3:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-9","title":"Exodus 15:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>I will pursue. Ge 49:27; Jud 5:30; 1Ki 19:2; 20:10; Isa 10:8-13; 36:20; 53:12 Hab 3:14; Lu 11:22 destroy. or, repossess. 14:5,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-10","title":"Exodus 15:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>blow. 14:21; Ge 8:1; Ps 74:13,14; 135:7; 147:18; Isa 11:15; Jer 10:13 Am 4:13; Mt 8:27 the sea. 14:28; De 11:4 they sank. 5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-11","title":"Exodus 15:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>like unto thee. De 3:24; 33:26; 1Sa 2:2; 2Sa 7:22; 1Ki 8:23; Ps 35:10; 77:19; 86:8 Ps 89:6-8; Isa 40:18,25; Jer 10:6,16; 49:19 gods. or, mighty ones. glorious. Le 19:2; Ps 89:18; 145:17; Isa 6:3; 30:11; 57:15; 1Pe 1:15,16 Re 4:8 fearful. Ps 66:5; 77:14; 89:5,7; 90:11; 119:120; Isa 64:2,3; Jer 10:7 Lu 12:5; Heb 12:28,29; Re 15:4; 19:1-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-12","title":"Exodus 15:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>stretchedst. 6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-13","title":"Exodus 15:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Thou. Ge 19:16; Eph 2:4 led. Ps 77:14,15,20; 78:52,53; 80:1; 106:9; Isa 63:12,13; Jer 2:6 guided. 1Pe 1:5 holy. Ps 78:54</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-14","title":"Exodus 15:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>hear. Nu 14:14; 22:5; De 2:4,5; Jos 2:9,10; 9:24; Ps 48:6 of Palestina. Isa 14:29,31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-15","title":"Exodus 15:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>dukes. Ge 36:40; Nu 20:14-21; De 2:4; 1Ch 1:51-54 Moab. Nu 22:3-5; Hab 3:7 all the. Jos 2:11; 5:1 melt. De 20:8; Jos 2:9; *marg: Jos 14:8; 1Sa 14:16; 2Sa 17:10; Ps 68:2; Isa 13:7; 19:1; Eze 21:7 Na 2:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-16","title":"Exodus 15:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>dread. De 2:25; 11:25; Jos 2:9 still. 11:7; 1Sa 2:9; 25:37 which thou. 19:5,6; De 32:6,9; 2Sa 7:23; Ps 74:2; Isa 43:1-3; 51:10; Jer 31:11 Ac 20:28; Tit 2:14; 1Pe 2:9; 2Pe 2:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-17","title":"Exodus 15:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>plant. Ps 44:2; 78:54,55; 80:8; Isa 5:1-4; Jer 2:21; 32:41 mountain. Ps 78:54,68,69; Jer 31:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-18","title":"Exodus 15:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Ps 10:16; 29:10; 146:10; Isa 57:15; Da 2:44; 4:3; 7:14,27; Mt 6:13 Re 11:15-17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-19","title":"Exodus 15:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>horse. 14:23; Pr 21:31 brought. 14:28,29; Heb 11:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-20","title":"Exodus 15:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>prophetess. Jud 4:4; 1Sa 10:5; 2Ki 22:14; Lu 2:36; Ac 21:9; 1Co 11:5; 14:34 sister. 2:4; Nu 12:1; 20:1; 26:59; Mic 6:4 a timbrel.{Toph,} in Arabic called {duff} or {diff,} and in Spanish {adduffa,} is the {tabret} used in the East; being a thin, broad, wooden hoop, with parchment extended over one side of it, to which small pieces of brass, tin, etc., are attached, which make a jingling noise: it is held up with one hand and beaten upon with the other, and is precisely the same as the tambourine.</p>\n<p>all the. Jud 11:34; 21:21; 1Sa 18:6; 2Sa 6:5,14,16; Ps 68:11,25; 81:2; 149:3 Ps 150:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-21","title":"Exodus 15:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>answered. 1Sa 18:7; 2Ch 5:13; Ps 24:7-10; 134:1-3 Sing ye. 1; Jud 5:3; Isa 5:1-30; Re 7:10-12; 5:9; 14:3; 15:3; 19:1-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-22","title":"Exodus 15:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>wilderness of Shur.This lay on the eastern shore of the Heroopolitic gulf of the Red Sea, and is still called the desert of Shur, according to Dr. Shaw.</p>\n<p>Ge 16:7; 25:18; 1Sa 15:7 three days. 3:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-23","title":"Exodus 15:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Marah. Nu 33:8 Marah. i.e., bitterness. Ru 1:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-24","title":"Exodus 15:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>14:11; 16:2,8,9; 17:3,4; Nu 11:1-6; 14:1-4; 16:11,41; 17:10 Nu 20:2-5; 21:5; 1Co 10:10; Php 2:14; Jude 1:16 What. 17:3; Ps 78:19,20; Mt 6:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-25","title":"Exodus 15:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>cried. 14:10; 17:4; Ps 50:15; 91:15; 99:6; Jer 15:1 a tree. 2Ki 2:21; 4:41; 1Co 1:18 a statute. Jos 24:21-25 proved. 16:4; De 8:2,16; 13:3; Jud 2:22; 3:1,4; Ps 66:10; 81:7; Pr 17:3 Jer 9:7; 1Pe 1:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-26","title":"Exodus 15:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>If thou. Le 26:3,13; De 7:12,13,15; 28:1-15 and wilt. De 12:28; 13:18; 1Ki 11:33,38; 2Ki 22:2; Eze 18:5 diseases. 9:10,11; 12:29; De 7:15; 28:27,60 for I am. 23:25; 2Ki 20:5; Job 5:18; Ps 41:3,4; 103:3; 147:3; Isa 57:18 Jer 8:22; 33:6; Ho 6:1; Jas 5:11-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-15-27","title":"Exodus 15:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>Elim.This was on the northern skirts of the desert of Sin, and, according to Dr. Shaw, two leagues from Tor, and near 30 from Corondel, which he conjectures to be Marah, where there is a small rill, which is brackish. He found but nine of the wells, the other three being filled up with sand; but the 70 palm trees had increased into more than 2,000.</p>\n<p>Nu 33:9; Isa 12:3; Eze 47:12; Re 7:17; 22:2</p>"}]}